      "en": {
        "title": "Your first reading collaboration",
        "summary": "Follow a sample from annotation and AI questions to verified prior knowledge, saved notes and a project handoff.",
        "headings": [
          "Choose a small, checkable result",
          "1. Add the sample text",
          "2. Save and retrieve an annotation",
          "3. Connect a model and ask a specific question",
          "4. Compare with a cited existing note",
          "5. Find the saved source note or hand off to a project",
          "Completion checklist"
        ],
        "html": "<figure><a href=\"/static/assets/tianshu/en/annotations.png?v=f10044bd6cf8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img src=\"/static/assets/tianshu/en/annotations.png?v=f10044bd6cf8\" alt=\"Your first reading collaboration — desktop app with isolated sample data, English interface\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1000\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Actual Shuvia desktop app · English interface, isolated sample data. Click to enlarge.</figcaption></figure><section id=\"part-1\"><h2>Choose a small, checkable result</h2><p>This exercise leaves you with an annotation you can retrieve. With a model connected, you will ask a question and compare the source with a cited existing note. Finally, you will locate a saved source note or a project handoff receipt. Use material you are comfortable testing and a separate directory; you do not need to organize your entire knowledge base first.</p><p><strong>Without a model:</strong> you can open supported local material, paste content, save and edit annotations, and adjust the theme and font size. AI questions, model analysis and automatic knowledge collaboration require an available model. <strong>A Shuvia account or login is not required.</strong></p></section><section id=\"part-2\"><h2>1. Add the sample text</h2><ol><li>Switch to Reading and choose Paste content. Use the title “Turn questions into checkable tasks.”</li><li>Paste this body:<blockquote>Advance one small goal at a time whose result you can check.<br>Keep the source text and its origin, then record your own questions.<br>State the goal and constraints first, then check the actual result.</blockquote>This text was written for the exercise; it is not a quotation from a published book.</li><li>Choose Connect. You should see all three paragraphs.</li></ol></section><section id=\"part-3\"><h2>2. Save and retrieve an annotation</h2><ol><li>Select “Advance one small goal at a time whose result you can check.”</li><li>In the nearby input, write “Try one small thing, then check whether its result meets the goal.” Press Enter.</li><li>Confirm that your thought appears to the right of that sentence. Click the mark again to see its color, line style and delete controls.</li><li>Switch to another material and back. Confirm that the annotation remains. You can also use annotation navigation to return to the original sentence.</li></ol><p>No model or knowledge base is needed for this step. You have saved a real reading record.</p></section><section id=\"part-4\"><h2>3. Connect a model and ask a specific question</h2><ol><li>Open Personal space → Models → Conversation and reading. Follow <a href=\"/docs/tianshu/models\">the model setup instructions</a> to test and connect your own provider.</li><li>Select the first sentence again and type “Explain how to turn a large goal into a small goal with a checkable result. Give an example.”</li><li>Press Ctrl / Command + Enter. Inspect the actual response and sources. If it fails, check the provider, quota and routing before sending again.</li></ol><p><strong>Know what is sent:</strong> a manual AI question sends the selected quotation, your question and the context needed to answer to your chosen model. An associated project may add project background and task summaries; a connected knowledge base may add matching excerpts from existing notes. Full-text analysis sends the text being analyzed. Automatic reading collaboration uses new marks or thoughts and relevant prior knowledge. Your model provider may process this content. Local storage does not mean content always stays on your device during a model call. Use material you are willing to send to that provider.</p><p><strong>Model charges are separate:</strong> API, model and external executor charges and quotas are set by their providers. Both connection tests and real questions may consume quota. This guide does not promise free use or a fixed price.</p></section><section id=\"part-5\"><h2>4. Compare with a cited existing note</h2><ol><li>Create a separate test knowledge directory containing <code>goal-breakdown.md</code> with this text: “For each task, define its deliverable, checking method and constraints before deciding the steps.” This is a practice note you supply yourself.</li><li>In Personal space → Knowledge base, select that directory for this exercise, choose an available model and save. Leave topic maintenance disabled if you do not intend to change topic files.</li><li>Return to the sample and ask “What does this passage add compared with my existing goal-breakdown note?” If retrieval finds nothing, check the directory and keywords; do not assume the model must find it.</li><li>Explicitly start content analysis from reading navigation. Select a claim with related prior knowledge and inspect its knowledge association card.</li><li>Check the existing note’s filename, exact quotation and comparison rationale. Expand context or full text and locate the original note. This step is complete only when you can check the source. A missing match or unlocated quotation is not a verified association.</li></ol></section><section id=\"part-6\"><h2>5. Find the saved source note or hand off to a project</h2><ol><li>Expand reading navigation. In the Source actions more menu, choose Organize this source’s notes to open the actual saved note. Automatic collaboration writebacks appear under Organize and hand off. Use View written note or View existing note to check the source and your original wording in the registered file.</li><li>Each source has one registered note file; subsequent expressions update that file. If the model finds no new knowledge, no new topic Wiki file may be needed. Your local annotation still exists.</li><li>To continue as work, first create a specific project. Use the reading handoff entry and explicitly request “Turn these three points into a checklist of verifiable tasks.”</li><li>Check the handoff receipt and open the destination project coordinator. Confirm that the quotation and instructions arrived. A todo count or finished executor alone does not establish acceptance.</li></ol></section><section id=\"part-7\"><h2>Completion checklist</h2><ul><li>Saved: the annotation reopens and can locate its original sentence.</li><li>Answered: you saw an actual model response and understand what was sent and who charges for it.</li><li>Cited: prior knowledge has a quotation and file source you can expand and check.</li><li>Located: the actual source note opens, or the project coordinator received the handoff.</li></ul><p>Without a model, complete the first two steps for now. Continue the later steps when your configuration is ready; do not present an unfinished project or association as successful.</p></section>"
      }
