      "en": {
        "title": "Personal account, appearance and advanced settings",
        "summary": "Your profile, local milestones, themes, text size and engine tools.",
        "headings": [
          "Appearance saves immediately",
          "Advanced settings · DSH",
          "Tools for the current conversation",
          "Help and replaying onboarding",
          "Personal account and local milestones"
        ],
        "html": "<figure><a href=\"/static/assets/tianshu/en/appearance.png?v=64c2455b0e6c\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><img src=\"/static/assets/tianshu/en/appearance.png?v=64c2455b0e6c\" alt=\"Appearance and advanced settings — desktop app with isolated sample data, English interface\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1000\" loading=\"lazy\"></a><figcaption>Actual Shuvia desktop app · English interface, isolated sample data. Click to enlarge.</figcaption></figure><section id=\"part-1\"><h2>Appearance saves immediately</h2><p>Open Personal space → Appearance → Interface language and choose Chinese (Simplified) or English (Preview). Interface labels change immediately; project names, source text, annotations and conversation content stay as written. The English preview covers common workbench views; some advanced tools keep their original language.</p><ul><li>Open Personal space → Appearance and choose System, Light or Dark. Work and Reading share a theme.</li><li>The reading font-size slider adjusts source text without changing toolbar density.</li><li>Expand annotation color names to name each of the five colors. Names save immediately; invalid or blank input is marked unsaved.</li><li>Apply the Core / Method / Evidence / Inspiration / Memorable quote preset, or restore color names. This does not move, delete or reclassify existing marks.</li></ul></section><section id=\"part-2\"><h2>Advanced settings · DSH</h2><ol><li>In the desktop client, open Personal space → Advanced settings · DSH.</li><li>Choose DSH native configuration to open configuration for Shuvia’s current engine.</li><li>Configure MCP, Skills, subagents or external executors according to their own requirements. This edits the same configuration for the current Host; it does not start a second engine.</li><li>Return to the original conversation and verify actual availability. An ordinary web preview does not replace the desktop native settings entry.</li></ol></section><section id=\"part-3\"><h2>Tools for the current conversation</h2><p>The tools entry in a Work conversation’s gear shows instruction files, MCP connections and Skills. Conversation-specific permission rules and model routing remain managed within that conversation.</p><p>Advanced configuration is for users with a specific need. To get started, you only need a model, a specific project directory or reading material; you do not need to configure every tool first.</p></section><section id=\"part-4\"><h2>Help and replaying onboarding</h2><p>At the top right, Help → User guide opens this manual. Replay onboarding starts from the first step. Esc closes the tour and remembers that you skipped it. After completion or skipping, it does not automatically open again in the same browser profile.</p><p>If browser local storage is blocked, the tour’s remembered state may last only for the current window. This does not affect annotations and conversations saved by the local service.</p></section><section id=\"part-5\"><h2>Personal account and local milestones</h2><ol><li>Open Personal space → Account. Work and Reading remain available without signing in. Once connected, the page shows your original nickname, masked email, account ID and actual connection status. A Chinese nickname is preserved when you choose English.</li><li>Use an available Google, Microsoft, GitHub or GitLab button to verify in your system browser, then return to the app to check and confirm the account. To link another provider, sign in to the original account first and use Manage sign-in and security to verify and link it. An available provider is not necessarily linked to this account; matching email addresses do not merge accounts automatically. Check linked identities in the account center.</li><li>Select View local milestones to see four first steps: send a conversation message, add a reading material with body text, save a reading highlight or annotation, and save a result. Each milestone is backed by records currently kept in this space. Missing records show No record yet; read failures show a retry state.</li><li>After adding or deleting records, select Refresh milestones or reopen the account page. Deletions update the counts. These are not lifetime totals, reading time or a measure of understanding; a highlight does not establish agreement with the source.</li></ol><p>Milestones are available without signing in, calculated locally and not sent to the account service. Signing out does not delete local materials. There is currently no cross-device milestone sync, paid membership or feature unlock tied to milestones.</p></section>"
      }
